# The repository stores every text file with LF, and WordPress Coding Standards
# requires LF in the files it checks. Without this, core.autocrlf=true hands
# Windows checkouts a CRLF working tree and `composer run phpcs` fails on every
# file before it looks at any real problem.
#
# Declaring the attribute here rather than relying on each developer's git
# config keeps the rule with the repository, so a fresh clone on any machine
# gets the same result.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.mo binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
